course: dictionary
lesson: 14610
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it, which are its context. «The poodle wagged its curly tail at the park gate.» Here a poodle is an animal, because it wags its tail and stands by a gate.
explain: Now read this: «Mr Jones's poodle agreed with every word his boss said.» Nobody means a real dog here. A poodle can also be a person who always obeys someone more powerful, and the words agreed with every word his boss said give it away.
explain: Ask yourself: does this make sense as a real animal, or as a person who obeys? Swap the meaning into the sentence and check. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Poodle is a noun, so you can write a poodle or poodles.
fact: «Poodle» can mean a dog with thick curly hair, often clipped into fancy shapes.
fact: Poodles come in toy, miniature and standard sizes.
fact: «Poodle» can also mean, informally and in the UK, a person or country that always obeys someone more powerful. It is said in a scornful way.
fact: The meaning you need depends on the context: a dog with a bow, or a person who always obeys.
exercise: «The poodle had a pink bow in its curly hair.» What is a poodle here? | A person who always obeys their boss | *A dog with thick curly hair | A small pink bow | A kind of new computer
exercise: «Sam is a poodle at work: he agrees with the manager about everything.» What does poodle mean here? | A bow on a shoe | A fast runner | *A person who always obeys someone more powerful | A large sort of dog
exercise: Which three sizes do poodles come in? | *Toy, miniature and standard | Mini, midi and maxi | Small, medium and large | Tiny, huge and giant
test: «The poodle sat on the rug and waited for its owner.» What is a poodle in this sentence? | A rug | *A dog | A person who obeys | A bow
test: «The small country was a poodle of the bigger power, doing whatever it was told.» What does poodle mean here? | *A country that always obeys someone more powerful | A kind of dog | A fancy haircut for a dog | A bow
exam: Which meaning of poodle is informal and used in UK talk and newspapers? | A dog with thick curly hair | *A person or country that always obeys someone more powerful | A toy shaped like a dog | A clipped hedge
